What does this program print?

```php
<?php
final class Box
{
    public function __construct(public int $n)
    {
    }
}
$a = new Box(1);
$b = $a;
$b->n = 5;
$c = clone $a;
$c->n = 9;
echo $a->n, $b->n, $c->n, "\n";
```

Using the same `Box` class, what does this print?

```php
function replace(Box $box): void
{
    $box = new Box(0);
}
function bump(Box $box): void
{
    $box->n++;
}
$x = new Box(3);
replace($x);
bump($x);
echo $x->n, "\n";
```

What does this program print?

```php
<?php
final class Ticket
{
    public static int $issued = 0;

    public function __construct(public string $seat)
    {
        self::$issued++;
    }
}
$t1 = new Ticket("A1");
$t2 = new Ticket("A2");
$t3 = clone $t2;
$t3->seat = "A3";
$t4 = $t1;
echo Ticket::$issued, "\n";
```

What does this program print (PHP 8.4 or later)?

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
final class Temperature
{
    public float $celsius {
        set(float $value) {
            $this->celsius = max(-273.15, $value);
        }
    }

    public float $fahrenheit {
        get => $this->celsius * 9 / 5 + 32;
    }

    public function __construct(float $celsius)
    {
        $this->celsius = $celsius;
    }
}
$t = new Temperature(-300);
echo $t->celsius, " ";
$t->celsius = 100;
echo $t->fahrenheit, "\n";
```

